   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the state finance law, in relation to the issuance of revenue bonds; and in relation to mental health service facilities financing; and authorizing the issuance of bonds by an authorized issuer for any authorized purpose; and providing for the repeal of certain provisions upon the expiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7847",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7847-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§68-b & 68-a, St Fin L",
    "lawSection": "State Finance Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7847\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the state finance law, in relation to the issuance of\nrevenue bonds; and in relation to mental health service facilities\nfinancing; and authorizing the issuance of bonds by an authorized\nissuer for any authorized purpose; and providing for the repeal of\ncertain provisions upon the expiration thereof\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis bill would extend, until March 31, 2011, two provisions of law\nand would authorize the Dormitory Authority of the State of New York\n(DASNY) to issue bonds that would be used to fund capital spending.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nThis bill would amend section 68-b of the State Finance Law (SFL), to\nextend (for one year) the authorization to issue Mental Health Bonds\nunder the Personal Income Tax (PIT) credit structure.\n\nIn addition, this bill would amend section 68-a of the SFL to extend\n(for one year) the ability of the DASNY and ESDC to issue Personal\nIncome Tax (PIT) Revenue Bonds for any authorized purposes.\n\nFinally, this bill would clarify DASNY's ability to issue debt without\nan Enacted Budget.\n\n STATEMENT IN SUPPORT AND BUDGETARY IMPLICATIONS :\n\nThis bill is necessary to enable the State to more effectively manage\nits cash position. The State issues $6 billion of bonds annually that\nare used to reimburse, or fund in the first instance, capital\nspending. In most cases, the State advances (loans) funds from the\nGeneral Fund or Short-Term Investment Pool (STIP) to fund capital\nspending, which is then reimbursed with bond proceeds. The initial\ncash outlay to fund capital projects reduces the State's cash\nposition. Currently, the State has spent $50 million from the General\nFund that cannot be reimbursed because bond proceeds are not\navailable.\n\nThis bill would allow DASNY, and other authorized State debt issuers,\nto issue bonds for the same purposes that were authorized in the\nprevious fiscal year. This authorization would allow DASNY to issue\nbonds, so timely reimbursement t an occur, improving the State's cash\nposition. In addition, this authorization would enable the State to\naccess credit markets at favorable times, providing an opportunity to\n\"lock in\" an attractive cost of capital.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
